WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.773
Alice shrieked with fear and anger as the pack of cards attacked her.

2
00:00:06.774 --> 00:00:13.847
"Stop that, you nasty things! Leave me alone!"

3
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:16.144
And then she woke up.

4
00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:20.781
Alice opened her eyes and found that she was lying by the river.

5
00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:24.056
Her head was in her older sister's lap.

6
00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:29.897
Charlotte was gently brushing away some leaves that had fallen onto Alice's face.

7
00:00:29.898 --> 00:00:36.859
"Oh, so it wasn't cards after all," Alice said slowly.

8
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.984
"What are you talking about?" Charlotte asked.

9
00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:43.223
She put down her book and stared at Alice.

10
00:00:43.224 --> 00:00:47.713
"You had a nice, long nap this afternoon."

11
00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:52.940
"I had the strangest dream." Alice sat up.

12
00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:55.455
"First, I was right here with you.

13
00:00:55.456 --> 00:01:01.715
Then a rabbit ran by, checking his watch and worrying that he was late.

14
00:01:01.716 --> 00:01:06.530
I jumped up and followed him down his rabbit hole."

15
00:01:06.531 --> 00:01:14.199
Charlotte laughed. "A talking rabbit with a watch! Oh, Alice.

16
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.910
You have a marvelous imagination."

17
00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.591
"The rabbit was wearing a colorful vest.

18
00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:25.059
And falling down the rabbit hole was only the beginning of my adventures."

19
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:29.447
Alice went on to tell Charlotte everything she could remember.

20
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:36.056
She had met so many odd creatures: the Mouse, the Caterpillar, the Cheshire Cat.

21
00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:39.817
"There was a queen who was always angry," Alice said.

22
00:01:39.818 --> 00:01:44.886
"If anyone did the slightest thing wrong, she shouted, 'Off with his head!'

23
00:01:44.887 --> 00:01:49.104
She even shouted, 'Off with her head!' at me!"

24
00:01:49.105 --> 00:01:53.068
"What did you do wrong?" Charlotte asked.

25
00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:57.589
"I don't remember exactly." Alice laughed.

26
00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:07.159
"But let me tell you more of what I do remember."

27
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.327
Alice finished her story.

28
00:02:10.328 --> 00:02:14.602
"That was a very strange dream," Charlotte said.

29
00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:18.812
"I'm glad you didn't really fall down that rabbit hole.

30
00:02:18.813 --> 00:02:22.858
But now it's time for you to run inside and have your tea.

31
00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:26.417
It's getting late, so off you go."

32
00:02:26.418 --> 00:02:34.355
Alice got up and ran off, thinking about her amazing dream all the way home.

33
00:02:34.356 --> 00:02:43.513
But Charlotte stayed by the river, watching the sunset and thinking of Alice's adventures.

34
00:02:43.514 --> 00:02:47.945
Soon she began to dream too.

35
00:02:47.946 --> 00:02:51.932
First, she dreamed about Alice as a little girl.

36
00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:56.347
Charlotte remembered Alice's voice and how she wore her hair.

37
00:02:56.348 --> 00:02:59.293
It was always falling in her eyes.

38
00:02:59.294 --> 00:03:03.560
Then she heard Alice's voice as it sounded today.

39
00:03:03.561 --> 00:03:10.176
After that the riverbank began to come alive with creatures from Alice's dream.

40
00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:16.636
The long grass rustled at Charlotte's feet as the White Rabbit rushed past.

41
00:03:16.637 --> 00:03:20.477
The Mouse splashed through the pool of tears.

42
00:03:20.478 --> 00:03:27.123
Charlotte could hear the teacups rattling as the March Hare and his friends talked and talked.

43
00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:31.950
The Queen of Hearts kept shouting, "Off with his head!"

44
00:03:31.951 --> 00:03:35.843
The pig was sneezing on the Duchess' lap.

45
00:03:35.844 --> 00:03:40.367
And the Mock Turtle sighed and sobbed.

46
00:03:40.368 --> 00:03:44.388
Charlotte continued to doze by the river.

47
00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:48.475
"Alice's Wonderland feels so real," she thought.

48
00:03:48.476 --> 00:03:56.750
"But if I open my eyes, there will be an explanation for all these sounds."

49
00:03:56.751 --> 00:04:02.057
She knew that the wind was rustling the grass, not the White Rabbit.

50
00:04:02.058 --> 00:04:06.032
A bird was splashing in the river, not the Mouse.

51
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:10.620
The rattling teacups were actually sheep bells.

52
00:04:10.621 --> 00:04:15.998
The Mock Turtle's sighs and sobs were cattle mooing in the distance.

53
00:04:15.999 --> 00:04:20.704
All the other sounds came from a nearby farm.

54
00:04:20.705 --> 00:04:25.822
Finally Charlotte dreamed about her little sister growing into an adult.

55
00:04:25.823 --> 00:04:31.568
She saw Alice as a grown woman who kept the loving heart of a child.

56
00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:36.818
Alice was gathering children around her and telling them many delightful stories.

57
00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:41.770
Some tales were about the happy summer days of her childhood.

58
00:04:41.771 --> 00:04:53.106
And others were about her adventures in Wonderland.

